{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Grace, I can help with this. Your account is active and not locked. I've requested a password reset, and it needs a technician to approve it before it goes through. Once approved, the technician will give you a temporary password by phone, not in an email. You'll be asked to set a new password the first time you sign in. If you'd like to avoid this next time, you can set up Duo MFA so you can reset your own password from the sign-in page.",
  "internal_note": "Verified sender is the account owner (user_id 11, Grace Okafor, Receptionist, active, not VIP, not locked, failed_login_count 0, sign_in_blocked false). Duo MFA: not enrolled, so self-service reset is not available. Request came from her own email address, so identity check per KB-002 is met. Queued reset_password for user_id 11 for tech approval. Tech: approve, then deliver the temporary password by phone to the number on file, not in the ticket. Temp password should force a change at next sign-in (per KB-003, change on Windows sign-in screen on office network or VPN, 14+ chars). Consider suggesting Duo enrollment. No unlock needed. Account is not disabled, so KB-005 does not apply.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-002",
    "KB-003"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
